      "created_at": "2015-04-09T17:59:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Adam\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/adam/48/1946_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Adam:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not sure if this still works, but you used to be able to use it to make instruction manuals and get a brick count, so you knew what pieces to order and how many:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://ldd.lego.com/en-us/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://ldd.lego.com/en-us/</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I believe it still does. I know I needed a prop for a tabletop RPG and decided to build it in Lego bricks, and this let me create and order exactly what I needed. My mind was blown…</p>",
